Now here is something that most retail investors get wrong and it cost me money before I figured it out.

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:25.380
Imagine you bought ARKK in January 2020 when Cathy Woods concentrated bets on innovation looked

00:09:26.340 --> 00:09:32.700
your order filled near $40. The ETF delivered a triple-digit gain that year on explosive moves in

00:09:32.700 --> 00:09:39.160
Tesla, Zoom and early genomics names. Then it posted a roughly 67 percent peak to trough drawdown by

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:45.800
late 2022 as rates rose and growth multiples compressed. ARK's thematic model relies on high active

00:09:45.800 --> 00:09:51.680
share and portfolio turnover often exceeding 100 percent. It channels capital into five core

00:09:51.680 --> 00:09:58.540
platforms including AI, robotics, energy storage, genomics, and autonomous vehicles. The thesis is

00:09:58.540 --> 00:10:04.620
that exponential technology adoption will drive outsized earnings growth over a five to 10 year horizon.

00:10:05.200 --> 00:10:11.040
In 2020 that produced spectacular returns. The subsequent drawdown illustrated how correlated

00:10:11.040 --> 00:10:17.320
these themes become during risk off periods. Wood sizes positions aggressively sometimes 10 percent

00:10:17.320 --> 00:10:23.100
or more in a single name and rebalance is frequently. This creates tax drag inside non-registered

00:10:23.100 --> 00:10:28.620
accounts. It also forces holders to endure volatility that exceeds the NASDAQ by two to three times

00:10:28.620 --> 00:10:34.400
on the downside. The biggest misconception with thematic disruptive investing is chasing last year's

00:10:34.400 --> 00:10:40.280
